      "id": 3,
      "text": "Between 1912 and 1920, the Loyal Hanna Coal and Coke Company of Philadelphia built the town’s core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://maps.roadtrippers.com/us/pa/points-of-interest/cairnbrook-historic-district",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cairnbrook’s mine remained in operation until 1958, marking the end of an era for the town’s industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://maps.roadtrippers.com/us/pa/points-of-interest/cairnbrook-historic-district",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic district preserves workers’ housing, commercial and social buildings, and a modern draft‑entry mine with its extractive structures.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://maps.roadtrippers.com/us/pa/points-of-interest/cairnbrook-historic-district",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Cairnbrook grew as a classic coal town, its fortunes tied to the region’s mining boom.",
